# Count Distinct Elements — Variable Interaction Diagram

**Array:** `[1, 2, 1, 3, 4, 2, 3]` | **k = 4**

---

## Variables

| Var | Role |
|-----|------|
| `i` | Window start |
| `j` | Current element in window |
| `o` | Look-back checker (i to j-1) |
| `k` | Window size |
| `count` | Distinct elements found |
| `arr` | Input array |

---

## Window 1 — `i=0`, window = `[1, 2, 1, 3]`

```
Index:  0    1    2    3    4    5    6
arr:  [ 1    2    1    3    4    2    3 ]
        ^                   ^
        i                  i+k (excluded)
        |←——— window ———→|
```

### j=0 → arr[0]=1, no o-loop (j==i), flag=true → count=1
```
        j
arr:  [ 1    2    1    3  | 4    2    3 ]
  o-loop: nothing to check
  ✅ count = 1
```

### j=1 → arr[1]=2, o checks arr[0]
```
        o    j
arr:  [ 1    2    1    3  | 4    2    3 ]
  arr[0]=1 ≠ arr[1]=2 → flag=true
  ✅ count = 2
```

### j=2 → arr[2]=1, o checks arr[0], arr[1]
```
        o         j
arr:  [ 1    2    1    3  | 4    2    3 ]
  arr[0]=1 == arr[2]=1 → flag=false ❌
  ✖ count stays 2
```

### j=3 → arr[3]=3, o checks arr[0],arr[1],arr[2]
```
        o              j
arr:  [ 1    2    1    3  | 4    2    3 ]
  arr[0]=1≠3, arr[1]=2≠3, arr[2]=1≠3 → flag=true
  ✅ count = 3
```

```
list.add(3)  →  result = [3]
```

